    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Blood is composed of plasma, serum, red blood cells (RBC), white blood cells (WBC), and platelets.",
        "Blood groups are categorized under the ABO system and Rh factor classification.",
        "The blood clotting mechanism works systematically to prevent excessive hemorrhage.",
        "The circulatory system relies on blood vessels and heart structure for continuous circulation."
